------------------------------\nMEM 10 x 500 mL | Buy Online | Gibco™ | thermofisher.com (https://www.thermofisher.com/order/catalog/product/es/en/31095052)\nciteturn46search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; MEM was developed by Harry Eagle, and was based on his earlier formulation of Basal Medium Eagle (BME). ... 31095 - MEM\n\nGibco™\n\n# MEM\n\nChange view\n\nCatalog Number  | Quantity\n--- | ---\n31095052 also known as 31095-052  | 10 x 500 mL\n\n2 Options\n\nCatalog number 31095052\n\nalso known as 31095-052\n\nPrice (EUR)\n\n232,00\n\nEach\n\n-\n\nAdd to cart\n\nQuantity:\n\n10 x 500 mL\n\nCustomize this product\n\nPrice (EUR)\n\n232,00\n\nEach\n\nAdd to cart\n\nMEM (Minimum Essential Medium) is one of the most commonly used of all cell culture media. MEM can be used with a variety of suspension and adherent mammalian cells, including HeLa, BHK-21, 293, HEP-2, HT-1080, MCF-7, fibroblasts, and primary rat astrocytes. We offer a variety of MEM modifications for a range of cell culture applications. Find the right formulation using the media selector tool.\n\nThis MEM is modified as follows:\n\nWith: L-glutamine, Phenol Red\n\nWithout: HEPES\n\nThe complete formulation is available.\n\nUsing MEM\n\nMEM was developed by Harry Eagle, and was based on his earlier formulation of Basal Medium Eagle (BME). Many other modifications of MEM followed, including Glasgow's MEM, MEM α, DMEM, and Temin's Modification. MEM is available with Earle's salts for use in a CO_{2} incubator, or with Hanks' salts for use without CO_{2}. This product is made with Earle's salts. MEM contains no proteins, lipids, or growth factors. Therefore, MEM requires supplementation, commonly with 10% Fetal Bovine Serum (FBS). MEM uses a sodium bicarbonate buffer system (2.2 g/L), and therefore requires a 5–10% CO_{2} environment to maintain physiological pH.\n\nFor Research Use or Further Manufacturing. Not for diagnostic use or direct administration into humans or animals.\n\nSpecifications\n\nCell Type Mammalian Cells\n\nConcentration 1 X\n\nCulture Environment CO_{2}\n\nManufacturing Quality cGMP-compliant under the ISO 13485 standard\n\nOsmolality 280 - 320 mOsm/kg\n\nProduct Line Gibco\n\nProduct Type Minimum Essential Medium (MEM)\n\nQuantity 10 x 500 mL\n\nShelf Life 12 Months\n\nClassification Animal Origin-free\n\nCulture Type Mammalian Cell Culture\n\nForm Liquid\n\nSerum Level Standard Serum Supplementation\n\nSterility Sterile-filtered\n\nWith Additives Glutamine, Phenol Red, Sodium Bicarbonate\n\nWithout Additives No HEPES, No Sodium Pyruvate\n\npH 7 to 7.4\n\nContents & Storage\n\nStorage conditions: 2-8° C. Protect from light.\nShipping conditions: Ambient.\nShelf life: 12 months from date of manufacture.\n\nMedia Formulations\n\n31095 - MEM\n\n## Frequently asked questions (FAQs)\n\n### Where can I find the osmolality for MEM Medium?\n\nThe osmolality is listed in the COA for the particular lot number of the medium.\nFind additional tips, troubleshooting help, and resources within our Cell Culture Support Center.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMorphologische Grundlagen aktivitätsabhängiger (https://ediss.sub.uni-hamburg.de/bitstream/ediss/204/1/Neuhoff.pdf)\nciteturn46search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; 31095 | Neuronenmedium MEM, Nr.\n6 Anhang\n89\n6.1.4 Medienzusätze\nZusätze Pferdeserum, 10 Vol.-% Charge: A 06228-495 | Hersteller Bioter\n--- | ---\nZusätze 3.3*10-3 mol/l Glucose | Hersteller Sigma\nZusätze 8.3*10-7 mol/l Insulin | Hersteller Sigma\nZusätze 1*10-3 mol/l Natriumpyruvat | Hersteller Sigma\nZusätze 3*10-8 mol/l Natriumselenit | Hersteller Sigma\nZusätze 2,3*10-5 mol/l Ovalbumin (Hühnereiklar) | Hersteller Sigma\nZusätze 2*10-8 mol/l Progesteron | Hersteller Sigma\nZusätze 1*10-4 mol/l Putrescin | Hersteller Sigma\nZusätze 1.28*10-6 mol/l Transferrin | Hersteller Sigma\nZusätze 2.5*10-6 mol/l 1-ß-D-Arabinofuranosyl-Cytosin-Hydro- chlorid (AraC) | Hersteller Sigma\n6.1.5 Angesetzte Medien\nPlating-Medium MEM, Nr. 31095 | Neuronenmedium MEM, Nr. 31095 | Neuronenmedium + AraC MEM, Nr. 31095\n--- | --- | ---\nPlating-Medium Pferdeserum | Neuronenmedium - | Neuronenmedium + AraC -\nPlating-Medium Glucose | Neuronenmedium Glucose | Neuronenmedium + AraC Glucose\nPlating-Medium - | Neuronenmedium Insulin | Neuronenmedium + AraC Insulin\nPlating-Medium - | Neuronenmedium Natriumpyruvat | Neuronenmedium + AraC Natriumpyruvat\nPlating-Medium - | Neuronenmedium Natriumselenit | Neuronenmedium + AraC Natriumselenit\nPlating-Medium - | Neuronenmedium Ovalbumin (Hühnereiklar) | Neuronenmedium + AraC Ovalbumin (Hühnereiklar)\nPlating-Medium - | Neuronenmedium Progesteron | Neuronenmedium + AraC Progesteron\nPlating-Medium - | Neuronenmedium Transferrin | Neuronenmedium + AraC Transferrin\nPlating-Medium - | Neuronenmedium - | Neuronenmedium + AraC AraC--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDissertation (https://online.medunigraz.at/mug_online/wbAbs.getDocument?pAutorNr=&pOrgNr=14011&pThesisNr=48711)\nciteturn46search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.3 years ago; Basal medium (500 mL bottle): MEM (Life Technology, REF #: 31095-029), DMEM ... MCF-7 medium: 50 mL MEM medium was pipetted out from the bottle into a fresh\n1.1.3 Polylysine solution \nThe stock solution was prepared by dissolving 100 mg polylysine in 100 mL water \n(either poly-L-lysine or poly-D-lysine can be used) and filter sterilize through a 0.22-micron \nfilter. \nThe prepared solution was pipetted into 15-mL falcon tubes, sealed with parafilm, and \nstored at -20 °C. Every time for coating glass plate, the solution was thawed up and mixed \nthoroughly, and after coating the falcon tube should be sealed with parafilm again and stored \nat -20 °C for further usage.  \n1.2 Medium \nAdditives: Fetal Bovine Serum (FBS Gold: PAA, Cat. #: A15-151-500mL; FBS HL1: \nSAFC Biosciences, Cat. #: 12103-500M), Penicillin-Streptomycin (Pen/Strep, Sigma, Cat. \n#: P0781), L-glutamine (Sigma, Cat. #: G7513), HEPES buffer (PAA, Cat. #: S11-001), \nSodium pyruvate (Sigma, Cat. #: S11-003), MEBM SingleQuot (Lonza, Cat. #: CC-4136) \nBasal medium (500 mL bottle): MEM (Life Technology, REF #: 31095-029), DMEM \n(Low Glucose) (Sigma, Cat. #: D6046), DMEM (High Glucose) (Life Technology, REF #: \n11960-044), MEBM (Lonza, Cat. #: CC-3151).  \n1.2.1 Normal medium recipe  \nMCF-7 medium: 50 mL MEM medium was pipetted out from the bottle into a fresh \nfalcon tube, then 50 mL FBS, 5 mL Sodium Pyruvate, 5.81 mL Pen/Strep were given into \nthe bottle. After mixing all the ingredients by shaking gently, the medium were filtered \nthrough a filtering system (Millipore, Cat. #: SCGPT01RE) which was screw onto an \nautoclaved 500 mL glass bottle. The bottle was screwed up with an autoclaved lid; \nHEK-293 medium: Stocks of FBS, Pen/Strep, and L-glutamine were thawed up in \nwater bath before preparation medium. 50 mL DMEM medium (High Glucose) was pipetted \nout of the original bottle into a sterile falcon tube. Then, 50 mL FBS, 5 mL Pen/Strep, 5.5 \nmL L-glutamine and 5.5 mL HEPES buffer (stored in 4 °C fridge) were given into the bottle. \nThen filtering process was the same as filtering MCF-7 medium;  \n23--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1 (https://publikationen.sulb.uni-saarland.de/bitstream/20.500.11880/40794/4/Maryam%20Amini%20thesis-library%20version.pdf)\nciteturn46search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; Blotting buffer 20% Methanol ... MEM Medium  \nFisher Scientific / 31095-029\nInflammasome sample buffer 1 x \n1 M Tris HCl pH 6.8 \nin H2O dest. \n \n10 mg Bromophenol Blue \n5 % β-Mercaptoethanol \n2 % SDS  \n25% Glycerol \nStacking buffer  \n0.5 M Tris-HCl  \nin H2O dest; pH 6.8 \n0.4% SDS  \nSeparating buffer  \n1.6 M Tris-HCl  \nin H2O dest; pH 8.8 \n \n0.4% SDS  \nElectrophoresis running buffer  \n250 mM Tris \nin H2O dest; pH 8.3 \n \n1.92 M glycine \n \n1% SDS \nBlotting buffer 20% Methanol  \n250 mM Tris-HCl  \nin H2O dest; pH 8.3 \n \n1.92 M Glycin \n1% SDS  \n20% Methanol \nTris-buffered saline (TBS 10x)  \n500 mM Tris-HCl  \nin H2O dest; pH 7.5 \n1.5 M NaCl  \nWestern blot primary antibody \n1% BSA  \nin PBS \n0.02% NaN3  \nWestern blot secondary antibody  \n5% skimmed milk in 1x TBS buffer plus 0.1% Tween \nTable 11 Cell culture buffers and media  \nBuffers  \nComposition/ Catalog number \nRPMI MEDIUM 1640 (CE) \n \nFisher Scientific / 11530586 \nDPBS  \n \nFisher Scientific / 14190094 \nMEM Medium  \nFisher Scientific / 31095-029 \nLymphocyte Separation Medium 1077 \nPromoCell / C-44010 \nHBSS, Hanks’ Balanced Salt solution \nH6648-6X500ML / Sigma \nErythrocyte lysis buffer \n155 mM NH4Cl \n10 mM KHCO3 \n0.1 mM EDTA (pH 7.3) \n0-5 mM Ca2+ buffer \n145 mM NaCl \n4 mM KCl \n10 mM HEPES (pH 7.4) \n10 mM Glucose \n40--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDOCTOR OF PHILOSOPHY (https://pureadmin.qub.ac.uk/ws/portalfiles/portal/234185400/CaV1.3_Ion_Channel_Expression_and_Hormone_Therapy_in_Prostate_Cancer.pdf)\nciteturn46search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; This cationic lipid formulation was used during siRNA mediated transfection ... Minimum Essential Media (MEM) (#31095, Gibco, Thermofisher)\nnot exceed 0.1% DMSO (v/v) to minimise risk of cellular toxicity. DMSO was also \nused as a cryoprotectant agent in freezing media preparations to preserve cellular \nintegrity during long-term storage of cell lines. The DMSO (%v/v) concentration used \nwas calculated from cell lines’ specification sheets. \nDulbecco’s Modified Eagle’s Medium (DMEM) (30-2002, ATCC) \nThis growth medium was used for sub-culturing the VCaP PCa cell line according to \nATCC culturing recommendations. This medium was supplemented with 10% FBS \n(v/v) and 1% Penicillin-Streptomycin (Pen-Strep) (v/v). \nFoetal Bovine Serum (#10270, Gibco, Thermofisher) \nThis growth supplement was used in all cell culture growth media, with the exception \nof RWPE-1 normal prostate cells, to provide the growth factors and hormones \nnecessary to sustain in vitro cell growth and survival. \n2% FBS \nThis was prepared using PBS and was used as a substitute for 10% FBS for \nneutralising trypsin during sub-culturing of the RWPE-1 cell line only.  \nCryopreservation medium \nCryopreservation medium was prepared according to recommendations provided in \nthe supplier’s cell line specification sheet where the percentage ratio of growth \nmedium, FBS and DMSO was outlined. \nHam’s F-12K (Kaighn’s Modification) (#21127, Gibco, Thermofisher) \nThis growth medium was used for sub-culturing the PC3 PCa cell line according to \nATCC culturing recommendations. This medium was supplemented with 10% FBS \n(v/v) and 1% Pen-Strep (v/v). \nLipofectamine RNAiMax Reagent (#13778, Invitrogen, Thermofisher) \nThis cationic lipid formulation was used during siRNA mediated transfection \nexperiments for the efficient delivery of siRNA molecules to in vitro cell lines. \nMinimum Essential Media (MEM) (#31095, Gibco, Thermofisher) \nThis growth medium was used for sub-culturing the DU145 PCa cell line according to \nATCC culturing recommendations. This medium was supplemented with 10% FBS \n(v/v) and 1% Pen-Strep (v/v). \n44--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTable of Contents (https://opendata.cemm.at/phd-alumni/Pazdzior_Robert_Kubicek_2022.pdf)\nciteturn46search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.0 years ago; MEM3 ... 3 (Eagle, 1959) - ThermoFischer Scientific media formulation #31095, MEM (ThermoFischer Scientific)\nINTRODUCTION \n(continued) \nInorganic Salts [mg/L] \nOther Components [mg/L] \n \nM1991 \nBME2 \nMEM3 \nDMEM4 \nRPMI \n16405 \n \nM1991 \nBME2 \nMEM3 \nDMEM4 \nRPMI \n16405 \nCalcium Chloride (CaCl2•2H2O) \n200 \n200 \n264 \n200 \n \n2-deoxy-D-ribose \n0.50 \n- \n- \n- \n- \nCalcium nitrate (Ca(NO3)2 •4H2O) \n- \n- \n- \n- \